  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COMMUNITY-BASED CONSERVATION OF JAVAN GIBBON (HYLOBATES MOLOCH) IN CENTRAL JAVA, INDONESIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO PROTECT AND RESTORE THE HABITAT AND POPULATION OF THE JAVAN GIBBON IN THE WESTERN PART OF DIENG MOUNTAIN THROUGH A COLLABORATIVELY MANAGED ESSENTIAL ECOSYSTEM AREA (KEE) AND A LANDSCAPE RESTORATION APPROACH. PROJECT OBJECTIVES INCLUDE, (1) MAINTAIN BIODIVERSITY IN THE WIDER MOSAIC FOREST LANDSCAPE BASED ON SOUND SCIENCE THROUGH RESTORATION OF FOREST AGROFORESTRY CORRIDORS USING ARBOREAL MAMMALS, SUCH AS JAVAN GIBBON AND LANGURS AS INDICATOR SPECIES (2) UPSCALE SUSTAINABLE COFFEE AGROFORESTS AND DEVELOPING SUSTAINABLE VALUE CHAINS FOR BIODIVERSITY FRIENDLY COFFEE USING A PARTICIPATORY MARKET-BASED APPROACH, WHICH WOULD POTENTIALLY LEAD TO 11 VILLAGES SURROUNDING THE AREA ADOPTING VILLAGE LAND USE PLANS THAT INCREASE FOREST CONNECTIVITY THROUGH COMMUNITY FORESTRY, AGROFORESTRY INTERVENTION AND COMMUNITY-BASED PROTECTION OF REMNANT FORESTS, AND AT LEAST 300 ADDITIONAL HOUSEHOLDS ADOPT COFFEE AGROFORESTS AND IMPROVED VALUE CHAINS FOR BIODIVERSITY FRIENDLY COFFEE AND (3) PARTICIPATORY GAZETTEMENT AND COLLABORATIVE MANAGEMENT OF A KEE, WITH THE FREE, PRIOR AND INFORMED CONSENT OF LOCAL STAKEHOLDERS, AND THIS WOULD LEAD TO A COLLABORATIVE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM ESTABLISHED FOR KEE.</narrative>
  </description>
